{"Enhancements", "Gameplay", "Gameplay", ""},
{"Enhancements", "Gameplay", "Custom and Randomizer Opponents", "Free Play's opponent choice also offers Custom (the Team Builder's enemy team) and Randomizer (a new army each match). Off: the game's six factions only."},
{"Enhancements", "Gameplay", "Random Map in the Map Lists", "Adds \"Random\" at the top of the Free Play and multiplayer map lists. It picks one of the listed maps that isn't banned (Balance > Ban Maps), mod maps included. Online, the host picks and everyone plays that map. Same setting as Ban Maps' \"A"},
{"Enhancements", "Gameplay", "Studs for Free Play Wins", "Adds this many studs to your profile each time you win a Free Play battle. 0: off (the game gives none). Not given online, while the computer plays your side, or with any red brick cheat on. The game holds at most 65,535 studs."},
{"Enhancements", "Gameplay", "LEGO Store Prices", "What the LEGO Store asks for each unit, in studs. Empty: the game's price. Applies to the store screens at once. Only this save's studs are affected, so it needs no host and no replay. Units with no price in the game (the King's starting ar"},
{"Enhancements", "Gameplay", "Game's prices", ""},
{"Enhancements", "Gameplay", "Start Position", "Where your army starts in Free Play. Automatic: the game's own choice. A start the map does not have becomes its last one. The computers take the other starts. Not used online."},
{"Enhancements", "Gameplay", "The AI Rebuilds Its Hero Every Time", "Normally the computer rebuilds its hero only once. On, it rebuilds it after every death. Free Play only."},
{"Enhancements", "Gameplay", "The AI Builds More Mines And Bridges", "Normally the computer builds one mine and one or two bridges. On, it builds a mine at every free mine spot it can reach and up to three bridges. Free Play only."},
{"Enhancements", "Gameplay", "The AI Builds Bridges On Any Map", "Normally the computer builds bridges only on maps that cut the land into five or more pieces, and then only when it needs one. On, it also bridges maps that do not need transports, once it has the builders, and keeps going up to eight bridg"},
{"Enhancements", "Gameplay", "The AI Builds Shipyards On Any Map", "The computer builds a shipyard only at the map's own AI build sites, and some maps with water have none, so armies whose special units are boats (Clipper, Brickbeard's Bounty, ...) never field them there. On, such a map gets build sites bes"},
{"Enhancements", "Gameplay", "The AI Finishes Tower Upgrades", "The computer keeps choosing the same tower to upgrade, and a new order cancels the upgrade already running, so long upgrades (Tower III, more so in FunLite2) rarely finish. On, a tower that is already upgrading is left alone until it is don"},
{"Enhancements", "Gameplay", "The AI Keeps Its Bridges", "Normally the computer retires a bridge that has stood unused for a while, even one it needs to reach you. On, it never retires a bridge. Free Play only."},
{"Enhancements", "Gameplay", "The AI Bridges When It Is Stuck", "When the computer keeps failing to reach the places it wants to build or attack, it builds a bridge at the free bridge spot nearest its goal, but only on maps with many AI build sites. On, it does this on every map, up to three bridges. It "},
{"Enhancements", "Gameplay", "The AI Builds Transports Only When Needed", "Normally the computer builds a transport on maps with many AI build sites even when it can walk everywhere, and the transport then sits idle, using one of its special unit slots. On, it builds a transport only when it needs to cross water, "},
{"Enhancements", "Gameplay", "Native Game Logic", "Late in big battles the game needs more than the DS's processor and runs slower than normal speed. On, the busiest parts of the game's own logic run as PC code, with exactly the same results, so the game keeps its normal speed. Off, the DS'"},
{"Enhancements", "Gameplay", "Faster CPU", "In the biggest battles a DS's processor cannot keep up and the whole game slows down. With this on, the emulated processor speeds up as far as the battle needs (up to four times a DS's), so the game keeps its normal speed; smaller battles r"},
{"Enhancements", "Gameplay", "AI Plays My Side (Spectate)", "The computer plays your side too, and you watch with the map revealed. You can still give orders. From the next battle. Free Play only, not online."},
{"Enhancements", "Gameplay", "Make All Builders The Same", ""},
{"Enhancements", "Gameplay", "Gold Rush target", "Bricks needed to win a Gold Rush match. Default 10,000. Online, the host's applies. Ctrl+click to type a number."},
{"Enhancements", "Gameplay", "Show every army's bricks in Gold Rush", "Shows each army's bricks against the target in Gold Rush."},
{"Enhancements", "Gameplay", "Fix the Monkey Cage", "Caught monkeys (Monkey Business) show the monkey cage the game has but never uses, instead of the Space Criminal's. Looks only."},
{"Enhancements", "Gameplay", "Prioritize Own Hero Spells", "With several heroes selected (say, yours and a hotwired one), the yellow brick shows your own hero's spells instead of whichever hero was picked first. Only changes your menu."},
